{"timestamp":"2026-08-27T09:24:01.668Z","ordinal":969,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a04288-9204-77f1-acd3-a30475a1451c","call_id":"call_7wrKqwCSvWFY85iCb05vfYf1","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"import torch\nfrom tiered_serve.dual_memory_loader.base import *  # noqa: F401,F403\n\n\n# Per-codec prefill-alt chunk thresholds: the crossover N* below which the\n# alt-decode path (H2D compressed exp + reconstruct) beats the raw_bf16 fast\n# path (H2D 2*M*K, no kernel).  N* = (T_h2d_raw - T_dec) / t_gemm_per_token,\n# and ONLY T_dec (the codec's full-weight reconstruct cost) is codec-dependent:\n# a cheap branchless palette decode (p4flat) crosses over at a large chunk,\n# while a heavy ANS decode (dietgpu) crosses over at a much smaller one.\n# (zipserv is triple-bitmap exponent coding, NOT ANS; under frozen_split its\n# exp-only decode is cheap too, so it crosses over late — see the table below.)\n# Measure T_decomp per codec with benchmarks/weight_compress.py on an idle GPU\n# (its d_ms decompress-latency column, summed over the qkv/o/gateup/down fused\n# weights), feed it through the slack model above, and paste the result here.\n# Codecs absent from this dict fall back to\n# _PREFILL_ALT_MAX_CHUNK_GLOBAL_DEFAULT (= prior single-threshold behaviour).\n# The env var TIERED_SERVE_PREFILL_ALT_MAX_CHUNK overrides both: a single int\n# forces one global threshold; \"<codec>=<n>,...\" sets per-codec values.\n_PREFILL_ALT_MAX_CHUNK_GLOBAL_DEFAULT = 1330\n# Threshold = (T_load_raw_bf16 - T_decomp) / T_gemm_per_token, i.e. how many\n# tokens of GEMM fit in the slack the raw-H2D path has over the decode path.\n# This is CONFIG-AGGREGATE, not per-weight: T_load_raw and T_decomp depend on\n# the residency layout, so the SAME codec has different thresholds in different\n# configs. The values here are for the frozen_split configs (cao family);\n#